# Java options of the amadeOS programs: every launcher in /usr/bin (amade-*, amadeos-*) passes this file to
# java first, so the options a program's launcher adds after it win (a larger heap for the Image Editor).
# Games read game.options instead. One option per line; changes apply to programs started afterwards.

# Memory. Java's defaults reserve a quarter of the RAM for each program and keep what it once used: the
# Software manager stayed at 600 to 800 MB after reading its catalog. A capped heap, the serial collector
# (short pauses on heaps this small) and giving unused memory back keep a program near what it needs.
-XX:+UseSerialGC
-Xmx256m
-XX:MinHeapFreeRatio=10
-XX:MaxHeapFreeRatio=30

# Start child processes with fork/exec instead of the JDK's jspawnhelper. An upgrade of the Java package
# replaces jspawnhelper under the running programs; they would then fail to start any process
# ("Spawn helper ran into version mismatch") until the next login.
-Djdk.lang.Process.launchMechanism=FORK
